From 020e9c0a79732d73b5c5aea7c9294e19c383ce18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:19:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the colour format on NVIDIA through
 NV_CONNECTOR_COLOR_FORMAT, and HDR as 4:2:2 at 12 bits where it is exact

Driver 620 gives the HDMI connectors of nvidia-drm its own NV_CONNECTOR_COLOR_FORMAT (auto, RGB,
YCbCr422, YCbCr444: nvidia-drm-drv.c; NVKMS refuses a request that it cannot take:
nvChooseCurrentColorFormatAndRangeEvo(), which the soft retry of the previous commit turns into
"Automatic" for that mode). "Colour format" (videoscreen.hadescolorformat) now uses it where the
connector has no "color format" of Linux 7.3; 4:2:0 has no value there, the driver chooses it
itself where a mode needs it, and the log says so once. Native Dolby Vision, an RGB tunnel,
captures the property and sets "auto" with its transport, and puts back what it found.

HDR above 8 bits as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits (issue 4: "I'll look at sending HDR at more than 8
bits as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits"): HDMI carries 4:2:2 at 12 bits in the clock of RGB at 8 bits, and
RGB at 10 bits needs 1.25 times that, which TMDS does not carry above 480 MHz, so on a sink that
declares no FRL (new CDisplayInfo::SupportsHdmiFrl(), HDMI Forum block) RGB leaves HDR at 8 bits at
4K50 and 4K60. There, with the existing opt-in "HDR at more than 8 bits"
(videoscreen.hadeshdrmorebits), a sink that declares 4:2:2 in its EDID, an HDMI connector, an HDR
request, and no colour format chosen by the user, the request that signals HDR carries YCbCr422
(OUTPUT_FORMAT::Hdr422Wanted(): any datum that is missing is "no"; a sink with FRL, where RGB can
go over it at 10 bits with full chroma, is not touched). The video is 4:2:0, so nothing of its
chroma is lost; what the head's conversion adds to the picture is for the user's RTX card to show:
not tried on hardware. The log says what was asked and what the driver did.

Host test of the rule in both directions (36 checks, mutations caught). Not on GPUs of driver 580.
